    "problem_statement": "Coroutine freezing not working in freezegun\n\nI'm using freezegun 1.2.2 with Python 3.10 and I'm having an issue with freezing time in coroutines.\n\nWhen I try to use freezegun with async functions, I get an AttributeError. Here's a simple reproduction script:\n\n```python\nimport asyncio\nimport datetime\nfrom freezegun import freeze_time\n\nasync def get_current_datetime():\n    return datetime.datetime.now()\n\n@freeze_time(\"2023-01-01\")\nasync def frozen_datetime_coroutine():\n    return await get_current_datetime()\n\nasync def main():\n    # This should return the frozen time (2023-01-01)\n    result = await frozen_datetime_coroutine()\n    print(f\"Result: {result}\")\n    print(f\"Expected: 2023-01-01 00:00:00\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    asyncio.run(main())\n```\n\nWhen running this script, I get an AttributeError instead of getting the frozen time. The decorator seems to work fine with regular functions but fails with coroutines.\n\nI noticed this started happening after updating to the latest version. It was working fine in previous versions."
